  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO2_NetworkServices_Q06
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why must a client be joined to the domain before it can use domain
    accounts?
  choices:
  - Domain accounts are stored on the client once it joins
  - It is only a licensing requirement
  - Joining installs Active Directory on the client
  - Only a member computer can ask the domain controller to authenticate a sign-in
  correctChoiceIndex: 3
  points: 10
  explanation: A workgroup machine has no trust relationship with the domain, so
    it has nobody to ask. It also receives no Group Policy, which is how everything
    later in this job order reaches it.
